# Enforce LF line endings for shell scripts on all platforms.
# Prevents CRLF corruption on Windows clones that would break #!/bin/bash shebangs.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Append-only session log — use git's built-in `union` merge driver so
# concurrent additions from different branches both land instead of
# conflicting. Removes the manual Accept-Both resync every batch PR needed
# on `## Unreleased` (MEH-985/986/959 sessions). Caveat: union keeps BOTH
# sides of a conflict hunk and may interleave line-adjacent edits — an
# acceptable trade for an append-only changelog (never edit old entries
# in-place expecting a clean 3-way merge).
docs/CHANGELOG.md merge=union

# MEH-991: Claude Design export is vendored reference material, not project
# code — keep it out of GitHub language stats and collapse it in diffs.
design-reference/** linguist-vendored
